  "Question": "Harry has \\(3\\) sisters and \\(5\\) brothers. His sister Harriet has \\(S\\) sisters and \\(B\\) brothers. What is the product of \\(S\\) and \\(B?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8 \\)",
    "B": "\\(10 \\)",
    "C": "\\(12 \\)",
    "D": "\\(15 \\)",
    "E": "\\(18 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Harry is one of the boys, so the family has \\(5+1=6\\) boys and \\(3\\) girls. Harriet is one of those three girls, so her sisters are the other \\(3-1=2\\) girls. Thus \\(S=2\\).\n\nAll six boys are Harriet's brothers, so \\(B=6\\). Therefore\n\\[\nSB=2\\times6=12.\n\\]\nThe product is \\(12\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
